Create src/modules/workspace/lib/reviewRequest.js exporting parseReviewRequest(body) via module.exports = { parseReviewRequest }. It validates the JSON body of the approve/reject API. It MUST import IMAGE_ACTIONS from './imageReview' (already implemented) and use IMAGE_ACTIONS.APPROVE and IMAGE_ACTIONS.REJECT as the only valid decisions - do not hard-code the strings 'approve'/'reject' in this file.
Return value is always a plain object:
- body is not a plain object (null, undefined, array, string, number): { ok: false, message: 'Request body must be a JSON object' }
- body.decision is not exactly one of the two valid decisions: { ok: false, message: 'decision must be "approve" or "reject"' }
- body.note present but not a string (and not undefined/null): { ok: false, message: 'note must be a string' }
- body.note, after trim(), longer than 500 characters: { ok: false, message: 'note must be at most 500 characters' }
- otherwise { ok: true, decision, note } where note is the trimmed string, or null when it is missing, null or empty after trimming. The success object must contain exactly these three keys.

