- 'dev-fixture' when env.NODE_ENV === 'production': { name: 'disabled', enabled: false, isFixture: false, reason: 'The development fixture provider is not available in production.' }
- 'dev-fixture' (not production) when env.WORKSPACE_ENABLE_DEV_FIXTURE !== '1': { name: 'disabled', enabled: false, isFixture: false, reason: 'The development fixture provider requires WORKSPACE_ENABLE_DEV_FIXTURE=1.' }
- 'dev-fixture' (not production) when env.WORKSPACE_ENABLE_DEV_FIXTURE === '1': { name: 'dev-fixture', enabled: true, isFixture: true, reason: null }
- any other provider name: { name: 'disabled', enabled: false, isFixture: false, reason: `Image provider "${value}" is not supported yet.` } where value is the configured string.
The production check wins over every other rule for 'dev-fixture'. Nothing here may ever enable a real (paid) provider.

